# ============================================================================
# .gitignore for SFL-EMB
# de Varda et al., "Behavioral and Brain Responses to Language Reflect
# Different Levels of Linguistic Representation"
#
# This repo holds ~114 GB of large data/model/derived files that must NOT go
# into git. The patterns below exclude them while keeping all CODE and small
# RESULTS files (results_*.csv, coefs, predictions tables, plots) tracked.
#
# The excluded files fall in two classes:
#   (A) REGENERABLE  - LM activation dumps, surprisal/embedding caches. These
#                      can be recomputed from the models + stimuli.
#   (B) RAW DATA      - fMRI subject arrays, audio, R data, raw timeseries.
#                      NOT regenerable -> back these up to external storage
#                      (OSF / Google Drive / cluster), do not just delete.
#
# For data you DO want versioned alongside code, consider git-lfs.
# ============================================================================

# ----- Python -----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/

# ----- (A) LM activation dumps (regenerable; the bulk of the 114 GB) -----
activations_*.json
*.parquet.gzip

# ----- (A) cached embeddings / surprisal pickles -----
embeddings/*.pkl
**/surprisal_*.pkl
**/activations_*.pkl

# ----- (A) per-model embedding dumps stored as extension-less files -----
natstor_fmri/embeddings/
probing_LMs/embeddings/
probing_LMs/XYdata/

# ----- (A) word-vector / model binaries -----
*.bin
*.bin.gz
cc.en.300.*

# ----- (B) raw fMRI subject data (~2 GB of .npy) -----
fMRI/fMRI/data_subject_*.npy

# ----- (B) audio -----
*.wav
natstor_fmri/sound_data/

# ----- (B) large raw data tables (back up externally, do not delete) -----
natstor_fmri/NaturalStories_TimeSeries_20220615.csv
control_fmri/data/brain-lang-data_participant_20230728.csv
*.rds

# ----- rendered notebook exports -----
*.html

# ----- vendored third-party repo, unused by current paper (has nested .git) -----
probing_LMs/SentEval/

# ----- OS / editor noise -----
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# ----- main_data/ is the curated input-data dir and IS tracked -----
# (overrides the broad rules above, e.g. *.rds, so natstor_maze.rds is included;
#  all files here are <100 MB, within GitHub's per-file limit)
!main_data/
!main_data/**

.claude/*
